- It lacks the empirical rigor and consistency of high-scoring optimization papers (e.g., `/home/wg25r/review_agent/human_reviews/AfhNyr73Ma.md` (7.0)).
- Because the empirical results undermine the theoretical claims, it falls below the "borderline" (4-6) range and closer to the "reject" range for papers with fundamentally unsupported claims.

